================================================================================
Modifications made for "Dreaming in Code"
================================================================================

The following changes were made to the NCC-UED Craftax baselines. They are stated
here to satisfy Section 4(b) of the Apache License 2.0.

1. Policy architecture replaced.
   The original implementations use a feed-forward policy. Both scripts here use the
   Gated Transformer-XL (GTrXL) policy imported from `dicode.transformer.transformerXL`
   — the same module DiCode itself uses. This is deliberate: the paper standardizes the
   underlying RL agent across all methods so the comparison isolates the curriculum
   mechanism rather than the policy class.

2. PPO hyperparameters changed.
   The argparse defaults were set to the paper's shared configuration (Table 6):
   learning rate 2e-4 annealed linearly, 1024 environments x 128 steps, 4 update epochs,
   8 minibatches, gamma 0.999, GAE lambda 0.8, clip 0.2, entropy coefficient 0.002,
   value coefficient 0.5, max gradient norm 1.0. These defaults are the values the
   published runs used.

3. Scope.
   Only the components used in the paper are included. The NCC method itself, other
   environments (MiniGrid, XLand-MiniGrid), and the deploy/analysis scripts from the
   upstream repository are not part of this release.
